# Insight: reusable E2E report (`y-ins-e2e-report`)

Use this rule when an E2E or manual-E2E run needs a final report artifact.

This is a shared report contract for:

- Unified ResiRoo and PMRoo E2E flows — entry `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e.mdc`; runbooks `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e-resiroo.mdc` · `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/test/y-tst-e2e-pmroo.mdc`

Invoking rules can add extra required fields for their scenario.

## Report artifact policy

- Output one **Markdown report file** per run.
- Save artifacts under **`cursor_workspace/`** (invoking rule can require a specific subdirectory).
- Do not overwrite previous reports.
- Filename must include **date + time** (`YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS`) plus a short scenario slug.
- If a value is not verified, write **`(not verified)`** explicitly.

## Required report structure (in this order)

Formatting rule for all sections:

- Any bullet or line that uses a `label: value` pattern must format the label in bold.
- Use this style consistently: `- **Label:** value`.
- Apply this to all report sections, not only the transcript section.
- Keep values unbolded unless another rule explicitly requires emphasis.
- Colons that are part of normal prose (not a `label: value` field) are allowed without bold labels.
- This applies to nested bullets too (for example under verification blocks).
- Do not leave unlabeled continuation lines under transcript or evidence fields.
- If a field value is multiline, either:
  - keep it on one line with explicit `\n` markers, or
  - continue on indented lines under the same bullet without creating a new unlabeled block, or
  - **(required when the value contains Markdown)** put the value in a **fenced code block** (use `text` as the language tag) on the lines immediately after the label.
- **Markdown-in-values rule (mandatory):** when a stored value contains Markdown-formatted text (for example a leading `#`/`##`/`###`/`####` header, `**bold**`, `> blockquote`, list bullets that would re-flow, or backtick fences), you **must** render it inside a fenced ` ```text ` block. Do not paste it inline as bullet text and do not escape characters one by one — the fenced block preserves the value verbatim and prevents the report’s outline from being polluted by embedded headers.
- Choose the smallest block that fits: only wrap the offending value (typically `Content`, `AIReasoning`, `Evidence`), not the whole message group.
- Always announce the block with a labeled bullet that ends with `:`, e.g. `- **Content (verbatim — fenced because the value contains Markdown):**`, then a blank line, then the fenced block.

### Run metadata

- Date/time (local timezone)
- Flow/rule used
- Environment (e.g. `Local + mp_mock (PMRoo)`, `testing MP`, `local docker`, `mixed`, etc.)
- Scenario name

### Goal and scope

- Goal of this run
- What was in scope
- What was out of scope

### What was executed

- Numbered steps actually executed
- Skipped steps and reason
- Key setup choices (for example queue, API base, debounce wait)

### Verification evidence

- API/UI proof lines with status codes where relevant
- Queue/worker/debounce evidence where relevant
- Database evidence where relevant
- Timeline/progress evidence where relevant

### Key identifiers

List all identifiers relevant to the run (only those that apply), for example:

- `woNumber`
- `jobToken`
- `workOrderId` / `ObjectId`
- `clientId`
- `locationId`
- message ids (`Message-ID`, inbox message id, message row id)
- conversation ids

### Results

- Expected behavior vs observed behavior
- Pass/fail/partial outcome per core expectation

### Issues, risks, and next actions

- Blockers or anomalies
- Whether each issue blocks the goal
- Exact next action

### Final outcome

- Final status: pass / fail / partial
- One concise conclusion sentence

### Summary (required as final section)

Include this section at the end of the report.

Summary section can include one or more test cases.
For each case, add a subheading with the test case code (for example `#### TST-BUG-001`), then include that case summary and transcript under it.

Summary must include:

- Test case code
- Environment label (single value; examples: `Local`, `Local + Mock`, `MP (Testing)`; include ingress when relevant: `Local / RabbitMQ`, `Local / Chat API`)
- Work order
- Pass/Fail result

For these three Summary fields, always render them as bullet lines (not a table):

- Environment
- Work order
- Pass/Fail result

Required bullet format:

- **Environment:** `<environment>`
- **Work order:** `<work order>`
- **Pass/Fail result:** `<pass/fail result>`

For conversation output in this section:

- Display each message from older to newer.
- Include each message date/time under label `Time` using concise format `DD Mon YYYY HH:MM:SS` (for example `19 May 2026 16:30:24`).
- Keep values verbatim (no cropping/shortening).
- Do not use fenced code blocks **except** when a value contains Markdown-formatted text — in that case the **Markdown-in-values rule** above applies and you **must** wrap the offending value in a ` ```text ` fenced block to keep it verbatim and stop embedded `#` headers from breaking the report outline.
- Do not display raw JSON format. (JSON or JSONB values should be flattened into `label: value` bullets, not pasted as a fenced JSON block.)
- Keep content human readable in markdown.
- Use **bold** style only for field labels, never for field values.
- Keep transcript blocks compact and easy to scan. Do not use one markdown row per field when compact grouping is possible.
- Do not add a wrapper label like `Message:` before grouped fields.
- Prefer grouped lines with separators (`|` or `,`) and bold labels, for example: `- **Message ID:** 2640 | **Role:** tool | **ConversationId:** 295 | **Time:** 19 May 2026 16:30:24`.

Preferred transcript style for this section:

- One message block at a time (resident/system/assistant as they occurred chronologically).
- `---` between message blocks.
- For assistant messages, include all relevant fields in readable form (for example MessageId, ConversationId, Response, State, Title, AISOWCompletion, AIReasoning, Evidence, IsEmergency, IsFrustrated, IsPhoneCallRequested).
- For assistant messages, place these two compact bullet lines immediately after the grouped message header line:
  - `- **State:** ... | **Title:** ... | **AISOWCompletion:** ...`
  - `- **IsEmergency:** ... | **IsFrustrated:** ... | **IsPhoneCallRequested:** ...`
- Do not add a parent bullet such as `Details:` for these two lines.
- When a transcript message includes attached or analyzed images (for example RabbitMQ `ImageUrls`, Marketplace uploads, or stored `messages.images`), add an **Images** field **after** **Content** (user messages) or after the other assistant fields for that block. Omit **Images** when the message has no images.
- **Images** format (use fetchable HTTPS URLs when available; resolve S3 `DocType` + `FileName` to public URL per `.cursor/y-generative-search/y-generative-search-rules/marketplace/y-upload-photo.mdc` if needed):

```markdown
- **Images:**
  - https://example.com/image-1.jpg
  - https://example.com/image-2.jpg
```

- List one URL per nested bullet under **Images:**; do not comma-join URLs on one line.

## Content and security rules (mandatory)

- Keep critical stored values intact (do not crop/trim `Response`, `AIReasoning`, `Evidence` when reported).
- Do not expose tokens, passwords, or secret env values.
- Include only non-sensitive evidence needed for verification.
- Keep language concise and professional (B2 English).
